Every clinician should explain an expected-opioid-benefit with a patient before an opioid-initiation and should explain a common-opioid-risk with a patient before an opioid-initiation and should explain a serious-opioid-risk with a patient before an opioid-initiation and should explain an opioid-alternative with a patient before an opioid-initiation.
Every clinician should explain an expected-opioid-benefit with a patient before an opioid-continuation and should explain a common-opioid-risk with a patient before an opioid-continuation and should explain a serious-opioid-risk with a patient before an opioid-continuation and should explain an opioid-alternative with a patient before an opioid-continuation.
Every clinician should ensure a meaningful patient-involvement in an opioid-start-decision.
